-- allium: 3
-- working-phase-visibility.allium
--
-- Working-Phase Visibility: Behavioural Specification
--
-- Scope: The client-side derivation of "what is the agent doing right
--        now?" from the composition of (conversation phase, connection
--        state, retry context, heartbeat freshness, first-byte received).
--        Defines how the StateBar's displayed activity is computed; the
--        lifecycle of the pending assistant bubble; the heartbeat
--        watchdog state machine; and the LastKnownActivity capture/
--        clear rules that prevent connection state from masking agent
--        state during reconnects.
--
-- Source of truth: this spec is a forward contract — the
-- wire/runtime changes listed under "implementation targets" below
-- are not yet present in the repo at the time the spec lands; the
-- spec is what the implementation will be built against. Existing
-- carriers (already in code) are listed separately.
--
-- Already in code (carriers reused by this spec):
--   ui/src/components/StateBar.tsx — derivation host
--   ui/src/conversation/atom.ts — phaseEnteredAt / toolStartedAt /
--       lastSseEventAt fields target landing spots
--   ui/src/components/MessageComponents.tsx — inline tool/bubble timers
--   crates/phoenix-ide/src/db/schema.rs — Conversation.state_updated_at
--       (already exists; this spec reuses it as the entry timestamp)
--
-- Implementation targets (this spec is a forward contract for):
--   crates/phoenix-ide/src/api/wire.rs — adds StateChange.state_updated_at
--       field and the LlmFirstByte SSE variant
--   crates/phoenix-ide/src/runtime/executor.rs — emits LlmFirstByte
--       from the token forwarder, injects per-tool started_at into
--       the assistant message's display_data.tool_starts map
--
-- Includes: DisplayedActivity composition; LastKnownActivity capture
--           on connected→reconnecting; HeartbeatWatchdog fresh/stale;
--           PendingAssistantBubble lifecycle; per-artifact inline
--           timer lifecycles.
-- Excludes:
--   - Server-side phase transitions (specs/conversation_atom/)
--   - Retry/backoff lifecycle and LlmAttempt event production
--     (specs/llm-retry-visibility/)
--   - SSE connection state machine (specs/connection_machine/)
--   - SSE wire envelope semantics (specs/sse_wire/)
--   - Per-message persistence and reducer logic (specs/conversation_atom/)
--
-- Cross-references:
--   specs/connection_machine/connection_machine.allium — ConnectionState
--       enum imported; transitions consumed by REQ-WPV-005.
--   specs/llm-retry-visibility/llm-retry-visibility.allium — sibling
--       spec; owns the canonical RetryContext value type and the
--       TurnRetryContext entity (keyed by conversation_id). This spec
--       imports it and references llm_retry/TurnRetryContext via
--       conversation_id lookups (same pattern as the conn/ClientConnection
--       cross-reference); the consumer's render_retry_modifier_for /
--       render_frozen_retry_modifier helpers compose the rendered suffix
--       from the imported value.
--   specs/sse_wire/sse_wire.allium — wire envelope contract; this spec's
--       new variants (LlmFirstByte) and field (StateChange.state_updated_at)
--       extend it.
--
-- Requirement traceability: REQ-WPV-001 through REQ-WPV-007 are modelled
-- here. REQ-WPV-008 (display continuity across reload) is a property of
-- the Init handling path and the sse_wire pending_truncated branch; it
-- is intentionally NOT modelled as a rule in this spec because it is
-- emergent from REQ-WPV-001's server-authoritative timestamps + the
-- pending_truncated degraded-display branch documented in
-- requirements.md. See `deferred Req008ReloadContinuity` below.

-- Spec-vs-code name mapping (consumed by every `conn/ClientConnection
-- ...state = live` use site below):
--   spec name      <->  UI code name (ui/src/hooks/connectionMachine.ts)
--   live           <->  'connected'
--   reconnected_display <->  'reconnected'
--   connecting | reconnecting | offline | disconnected  <->  same
-- The "healthy enough that absence of events is suspicious" set used
-- by REQ-WPV-004 is { live } (spec) == { 'connected' } (code). The
-- brief grace state `reconnected_display` / 'reconnected' is excluded
-- so the watchdog doesn't duplicate the connection chip's messaging.
use "../connection_machine/connection_machine.allium" as conn
use "../llm-retry-visibility/llm-retry-visibility.allium" as llm_retry

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Actor Declarations
------------------------------------------------------------

-- The user whose browser is rendering the conversation. Identity scope
-- is "one tab"; multiple tabs viewing the same conversation each have
-- their own ClientView instance and derive the same DisplayedActivity
-- independently from the shared server-authoritative timestamps.
--
-- `conversation_id` is carried so cross-spec entity lookups into the
-- connection_machine spec (whose ClientConnection entity is keyed by
-- `conversation_id`, not by view) are well-formed: e.g.
-- `conn/ClientConnection{conversation_id: view.conversation_id}`.
actor ClientView {
    identified_by: Integer
    conversation_id: String
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Value Types
------------------------------------------------------------

-- A snapshot of the most recent SSE event arrival on this client.
-- Bumped on every event of any kind, including the typed `ping`
-- keep-alive (REQ-WPV-004). Pure client-side clock.
value EventClock {
    last_event_at: Timestamp  -- client clock, unix ms
}

-- A frozen capture of the agent's activity at the moment we lost
-- connection. The `elapsed_ms_at_disconnect` field is computed once at
-- capture time so the display shows a stable number through the
-- reconnect, rather than continuing to count forward through a period
-- where we have no signal from the server.
--
-- `retry` carries any unresolved retry context that was visible at the
-- moment we degraded (REQ-WPV-003: the retry modifier is part of the
-- most-specific known activity). Without it the reconnect display
-- would silently drop `(retry 2/5)` from a frozen "last: thinking 12s"
-- even though that was the most specific signal we had — which is
-- exactly the "connection state masking agent state" failure REQ-WPV-005
-- forbids.
value LastKnownActivity {
    phase:                 WorkingPhase
    base_reason_text:      String
    elapsed_ms_at_disconnect: Integer
    captured_at:           Timestamp
    retry:                 llm_retry/RetryContext?
}

-- The fully-composed text + visual treatment shown in the StateBar.
-- Produced by the derivation rules below from the entity inputs.
value DisplayedActivity {
    text:        String      -- the user-visible string
    dot_class:   DotClass    -- visual treatment of the state dot
    has_timer:   Boolean     -- whether `text` contains a live elapsed
                             -- counter that should re-render each second
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Enumerations
------------------------------------------------------------

-- The subset of conversation phases that are "working." Used as the
-- discriminator for whether to display a live timer and whether the
-- heartbeat watchdog is armed. The complement (idle, terminal,
-- handed_off, awaiting_*, error, context_exhausted) is grouped here
-- as `not_working` for completeness; this spec governs display only
-- when the phase IS working.
--
-- Source-of-truth lives in the runtime ConvState enum; this enum
-- mirrors only the working-vs-not distinction.
enum WorkingPhase {
    llm_requesting          -- includes the seeded and awaiting_llm variants
    | tool_executing
    | awaiting_sub_agents
    | awaiting_continuation
    | cancelling             -- cancelling/cancelling_tool/cancelling_sub_agents
    | awaiting_recovery
}

-- The visual treatment class applied to the StateBar's status dot.
-- Mirrors the dot-class CSS conventions already in use at
-- the `stateText` composition block in StateBar.tsx.
enum DotClass {
    idle
    | working
    | approval
    | error
    | terminal
    | connecting
    | reconnecting
    | offline
    | reconnected
    | hidden
    | degraded   -- new: watchdog has fired
}

-- Watchdog freshness. `fresh` = an SSE event arrived within
-- HEARTBEAT_WATCHDOG_SECONDS; `stale` = it has not. The watchdog only
-- arms while the conversation is in a working phase AND the connection
-- state is `live` (per conn/ConnectionState). Outside those conditions
-- it remains `fresh` by definition.
enum HeartbeatFreshness {
    fresh
    | stale
}

-- Lifecycle of the placeholder assistant bubble that appears during
-- llm_requesting with no tokens yet. The bubble is a reusable
-- singleton: it returns to `not_present` after each turn so the next
-- turn can re-arm it. `not_present` is the idle ground state; the
-- "complete" outcome (assistant message persisted) and the "removed"
-- outcome (phase exited without tokens) both route back to
-- `not_present` rather than terminal states.
enum PendingBubbleState {
    not_present
    | placeholder
    | streaming
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Entities
------------------------------------------------------------

-- The conversation phase as observed by this client.
-- `state_updated_at` is server-authoritative (REQ-WPV-001); on Init it
-- comes from `EnrichedConversation.state_updated_at` (the existing
-- top-level field, flattened from `Conversation`); on each StateChange
-- it is carried on the new `StateChange.state_updated_at` field. The
-- entity has no field-level
-- transitions because each StateChange / Init replaces the snapshot
-- wholesale — there is no meaningful intermediate state to model.
entity ObservedPhase {
    view: ClientView

    -- Whether the phase is one of the working phases. When working = false
    -- (idle, terminal, etc.) the DisplayedActivity derivation skips the
    -- working-phase rules entirely.
    working: Boolean

    -- The specific working phase, when working.
    phase: WorkingPhase?

    -- Server-authoritative entry time. Sourced from the existing
    -- `Conversation.state_updated_at: DateTime<Utc>` field (which the
    -- runtime already bumps on every state transition, see db.rs:676);
    -- this entity uses the same value, just normalised to unix ms. The
    -- single source for elapsed-time displays. NEVER set client-side
    -- from event arrival time.
    state_updated_at: Timestamp
}

-- The pending placeholder bubble. Singleton per ClientView. DOM presence
-- is gated on state in { placeholder, streaming } (the streaming state
-- still holds the same bubble; only its contents change from elapsed-
-- counter to streamed text per REQ-WPV-002). After a turn completes the
-- bubble returns to `not_present` so the next turn can re-arm it — the
-- state machine is reusable across turns, not single-shot.
entity PendingAssistantBubble {
    view: ClientView

    state: PendingBubbleState

    -- The request_id of the LLM request this bubble is bound to. The
    -- placeholder bubble is created BEFORE we know which request_id the
    -- forwarder will assign — the value is set when LlmFirstByte
    -- arrives carrying that id (PendingBubbleTransitionsToStreaming
    -- rule below) and cleared on return to not_present. Null during
    -- the `placeholder` phase; non-null during `streaming`.
    request_id: String?

    -- Server-authoritative; matches ObservedPhase.state_updated_at when
    -- the bubble is in `placeholder` state. Used for the inline elapsed
    -- counter inside the bubble.
    placeholder_since: Timestamp?

    -- The SSE sequence_id stored on the bubble to correlate the
    -- persisted assistant Message back to this bubble's request. Set
    -- to the LlmFirstByte event's own sequence_id on the streaming
    -- transition. Per sse_wire.allium, each SSE event carries its own
    -- monotonic sequence_id from SseBroadcaster.next_seq, so LlmFirstByte
    -- and the first Token that follows it have DIFFERENT consecutive
    -- sequence_ids (LlmFirstByte is emitted immediately before the
    -- first Token, taking one seq; the Token takes the next). Both are
    -- strictly greater than any prior event for this conversation, so
    -- a Message event with seq > first_byte_seq is unambiguously this
    -- bubble's completion. SseWireEvent::Message does NOT carry the
    -- request_id, so wire-level request_id correlation is unavailable
    -- and this seq-based form is the only reliable correlator.
    first_byte_seq: Integer?

    transitions state {
        not_present -> placeholder
        placeholder -> streaming
        placeholder -> not_present
        streaming -> not_present
    }
}

-- The per-tool inline timer carrier. One per running tool. Lives only
-- while the tool-use block exists without a tool-result; once the
-- result lands, this entity is removed and the existing duration_ms
-- on the result takes over.
entity InflightToolTimer {
    view: ClientView

    -- The tool_use_id of the tool whose timer this is. Conversation-
    -- unique by construction (same as elsewhere in the runtime).
    tool_use_id: String

    -- Server-authoritative start time. Carrier: the parent assistant
    -- message's `display_data.tool_starts` map (a HashMap<ToolUseId,
    -- unix_ms>) populated by the runtime when `dispatch_tool_execution`
    -- begins and propagated via `MessageUpdated`. This avoids amending
    -- the persisted `ContentBlock::ToolUse` schema (which has only
    -- {id, name, input}); see design.md "Per-tool started_at carrier."
    started_at: Timestamp
}

-- The StateBar's derived activity output. One per ClientView. Updated
-- in-place by the DisplayWhen* derivation rules each time
-- DerivationTriggered(view) fires.
entity StateBarDisplay {
    view: ClientView
    activity: DisplayedActivity
}

-- Watchdog freshness state. Single instance per ClientView.
entity HeartbeatWatchdog {
    view: ClientView

    freshness: HeartbeatFreshness

    -- Updated on every SSE event of any kind (including typed `ping`
    -- keep-alive).
    last_event_at: Timestamp

    transitions freshness {
        fresh -> stale
            -- Conditions checked once per tick (see WatchdogTick rule):
            --   conn.state = live
            --   AND ObservedPhase.working = true
            --   AND now() - last_event_at >= HEARTBEAT_WATCHDOG_SECONDS
        stale -> fresh
            -- Any SSE event arrives, OR conn.state leaves live (which
            -- already conveys the channel problem via the connection
            -- chip; the watchdog disarms to avoid duplicate messaging).
    }
}

-- The captured snapshot at the moment we left `live`. Cleared the
-- moment a fresh Init lands (which carries the authoritative current
-- phase + state_updated_at).
entity LastKnownActivityCapture {
    view: ClientView

    captured: LastKnownActivity?  -- absent when there is nothing to remember
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Config
------------------------------------------------------------

config {
    heartbeat_watchdog_seconds: Integer = 35
    -- ~2.3x the server's SSE keep-alive interval (15s; api/sse.rs:71,
    -- handlers.rs). One missed keep-alive must not trigger the
    -- watchdog.

    watchdog_tick_interval_ms: Integer = 1000
    -- How often the watchdog re-checks last_event_at against the
    -- threshold. Same cadence as the per-second elapsed counters so
    -- one timer drives both displays.
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Helpers (pure functions referenced by the rules below)
------------------------------------------------------------
--
-- Allium has no formal helper-function declaration; the rules below
-- call these by bare identifier. This block is the single source of
-- truth for their signatures and semantics. Any rule that uses a name
-- not in this block is using an undeclared helper — call that out in
-- review rather than inventing semantics ad-hoc.
--
-- Phase mapping (ConvState → WorkingPhase enum):
--
--   is_working_phase(raw_state: ConvState) -> Boolean
--       True iff raw_state is one of the runtime ConvState variants
--       that maps to our WorkingPhase enum (llm_requesting variants,
--       tool_executing, awaiting_sub_agents, awaiting_continuation,
--       cancelling variants, awaiting_recovery). False for idle,
--       terminal, error, context_exhausted, handed_off, etc.
--
--   working_phase_of(raw_state: ConvState) -> WorkingPhase?
--       The mapped WorkingPhase value when is_working_phase(raw_state)
--       holds; null otherwise. Mapping detailed in the
--       ObservedPhaseUpdatedByStateChange rule's @guidance.
--
-- Display-text formatters (return DisplayedActivity or String):
--
--   base_reason_text_for(phase: ObservedPhase) -> String
--       The leading prose for the base reason, e.g. "thinking",
--       "executing bash", "awaiting sub-agents". Does NOT include the
--       elapsed counter; just the verb-phrase.
--
--   phase_prose(p: WorkingPhase) -> String
--       Map from a specific WorkingPhase value to its display prose
--       for the "other working" catch-all (awaiting_sub_agents,
--       awaiting_continuation, cancelling, awaiting_recovery). Pure
--       function; does not look up tool names.
--
--   connection_only_display(state: conn/ConnectionState,
--                           attempts: Integer) -> DisplayedActivity
--       The connection-chip-only display used when there is no agent
--       activity to surface alongside (reconnecting/offline without
--       captured activity, plus the transient connecting /
--       reconnected_display / disconnected states). Encodes
--       text + dot_class + has_timer=false.
--
--   non_working_display(phase: ObservedPhase) -> DisplayedActivity
--       The idle / terminal / approval / error display. text reads
--       the static phase label (e.g. "idle", "context exhausted");
--       dot_class is the per-phase visual treatment; has_timer=false.
--
--   render_retry_modifier_for(view: ClientView) -> String
--       "" when no llm_retry/TurnRetryContext{conversation_id:
--       view.conversation_id} exists; " (retry K/N <reason>)" when
--       one does. Leading space so the suffix concatenates cleanly
--       onto a base reason text. K is retry.attempt, N is
--       retry.max_attempts, <reason> comes from retry.reason_text.
--       The TurnRetryContext entity itself is owned by the
--       llm-retry-visibility sibling spec (keyed by conversation_id);
--       this helper does the lookup via view.conversation_id, the
--       same cross-spec pattern used for conn/ClientConnection.
--
--   render_frozen_retry_modifier(retry: llm_retry/RetryContext?) -> String
--       "" when retry is null; same " (retry K/N <reason>)" format
--       as render_retry_modifier_for otherwise. Reads from a frozen
--       LastKnownActivity.retry snapshot rather than the live
--       TurnRetryContext, so the reconnect display surfaces the
--       retry context that was visible at disconnect time.
--
--   str(n: Integer) -> String
--       Standard integer-to-decimal-string formatting. Used inline
--       in DisplayedActivity.text construction.
--
-- State lookups:
--
--   current_tool_name(view: ClientView) -> String
--       The display name of the most-recently-started InflightToolTimer
--       for the given view. InflightToolTimer itself only stores
--       (view, tool_use_id, started_at); the name is resolved by
--       joining the timer's tool_use_id with the matching
--       ContentBlock::ToolUse{id, name, input} on the assistant
--       message (the runtime persists tool-use blocks by id, and the
--       client already has them via the message list).
--       Precondition: at least one InflightToolTimer exists for the
--       view — enforced by the caller (DisplayWhenToolExecutingWithTimer
--       gates on `exists InflightToolTimer{view: view}`). The
--       complementary DisplayWhenToolExecutingNoTimerYet rule covers
--       the brief window between the `tool_executing` state_change
--       and the MessageUpdated that creates the timer; that rule
--       does not call this helper. Parallel-tool policy is deferred
--       (see `deferred MultipleParallelToolsInOneAssistantMessage`).
--
--   current_retry_for(view: ClientView) -> llm_retry/RetryContext?
--       llm_retry/TurnRetryContext{conversation_id:
--       view.conversation_id}.retry when the entity exists; null
--       otherwise. The LastKnownActivity capture rule uses this to
--       snapshot retry alongside the base activity at the moment of
--       degrade.
--
-- Invariant predicates (used only inside `invariant` blocks):
--
--   live_timer_count_in(text: String) -> Integer
--       Count of distinct live elapsed-counter occurrences inside a
--       rendered display string. The format is "<reason> Ns" where N
--       is a positive integer followed by 's' (and possibly a retry
--       suffix). The helper does NOT match "(retry 2/5)" as a
--       counter — the elapsed is the unprefixed " Ns" token before
--       the optional retry parenthetical.
--
--   elapsed_values_in(display: StateBarDisplay) -> Set<ElapsedValue>
--       All elapsed-value tokens that appear in the display, each
--       annotated with a `.source` field that traces back to one of
--       the server-authoritative timestamps allowed by the
--       ElapsedTracesToServerTimestamp invariant.
--
--   most_recent_event_was_init(view: ClientView) -> Boolean
--       True iff the most recent SSE event delivered to the client
--       view was an Init (any variant). Used by the
--       InitClearsCapturedActivity invariant to assert wipe-on-init
--       semantics structurally.
--
------------------------------------------------------------

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Rules — ObservedPhase
------------------------------------------------------------

-- REQ-WPV-001: a StateChange replaces the ObservedPhase wholesale.
-- Event shape (positional): SseStateChangeReceived(view, raw_state,
-- state_updated_at). `raw_state` is the opaque ConvState the server
-- emits; the helpers `is_working_phase` and `working_phase_of`
-- (described in @guidance) project it onto our WorkingPhase enum.
-- `state_updated_at` is the value of `Conversation.state_updated_at`
-- at the moment the new state took effect — the runtime already
-- bumps this on every transition (db.rs:676), this rule just
-- propagates it onto the client snapshot.
rule ObservedPhaseUpdatedByStateChange {
    when: SseStateChangeReceived(view, raw_state, state_updated_at)

    ensures: ObservedPhase{view}.working    = is_working_phase(raw_state)
    ensures: ObservedPhase{view}.phase      = working_phase_of(raw_state)
    ensures: ObservedPhase{view}.state_updated_at = state_updated_at

    @guidance
        -- is_working_phase / working_phase_of map the runtime ConvState
        -- variants to our WorkingPhase enum. The mapping is:
        --   llm_requesting | awaiting_llm | seeded_llm_requesting
        --     -> WorkingPhase.llm_requesting
        --   tool_executing -> WorkingPhase.tool_executing
        --   awaiting_sub_agents -> awaiting_sub_agents
        --   awaiting_continuation -> awaiting_continuation
        --   cancelling | cancelling_tool | cancelling_sub_agents
        --     -> cancelling
        --   awaiting_recovery -> awaiting_recovery
        --   (anything else) -> working = false; phase null.
        --
        -- When working = false, the `phase` field is left null by the
        -- implementation; consumers must check `working` before reading.
}

-- REQ-WPV-001: Init's phase carries the same state_updated_at field;
-- on (re-)connect, the ObservedPhase is reconstructed from it. The
-- carrier on the wire is the existing `Conversation.state_updated_at`
-- field flattened into `EnrichedConversation` at the top level of the
-- Init payload — no new struct, no parallel representation.
-- Event shape: SseInitReceived(view, raw_state, state_updated_at,
-- pending_truncated). `pending_truncated` is unused here (this rule
-- only cares about the current state + entry time, which are
-- authoritative regardless of ring-overflow status), but the event
-- shape is shared with PendingBubbleSeededFromInit below which DOES
-- consume it; declaring the full positional signature keeps all
-- consumers aligned.
rule ObservedPhaseSeededFromInit {
    when: SseInitReceived(view, raw_state, state_updated_at, pending_truncated)

    ensures: ObservedPhase{view}.working    = is_working_phase(raw_state)
    ensures: ObservedPhase{view}.phase      = working_phase_of(raw_state)
    ensures: ObservedPhase{view}.state_updated_at = state_updated_at
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Rules — HeartbeatWatchdog
------------------------------------------------------------

-- Any SSE event (including the typed `ping` keep-alive) updates
-- last_event_at and resets freshness to fresh.
-- Event shape: SseAnyEventReceived(view) — fanned in from per-event
-- listeners (see @guidance below).
rule WatchdogResetOnAnyEvent {
    when: SseAnyEventReceived(view)

    ensures: HeartbeatWatchdog{view}.last_event_at = now()
    ensures: HeartbeatWatchdog{view}.freshness     = fresh

    @guidance
        -- Native `EventSource` does NOT have a catch-all for named SSE
        -- events; named events only fire listeners registered for that
        -- specific event name (see MDN, "Using server-sent events":
        -- https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Server-sent_events/Using_server-sent_events).
        -- The default `onmessage` only fires for events with no event
        -- name (the unnamed "message" event).
        --
        -- The implementation MUST therefore register an explicit
        -- listener for every named event the server emits, AND each
        -- listener must bump `lastSseEventAt` (this rule's effect)
        -- before delegating to per-event-type processing. The current
        -- event set, sourced from `SseWireEvent::event_type()` in
        -- `crates/phoenix-ide/src/api/wire.rs`:
        --
        --   init, message, message_updated, state_change, token,
        --   agent_done, conversation_became_terminal,
        --   conversation_update, error, browser_session_state,
        --   steer_message_queued, rate_limit_snapshot,
        --   conversation_hard_deleted
        --
        -- Plus the new variants this spec introduces:
        --
        --   llm_first_byte (working-phase-visibility)
        --   llm_attempt    (llm-retry-visibility, sibling spec)
        --   ping           (server keep-alive, see design.md
        --                   "Server keep-alive observation")
        --
        -- A small wrapper helper in the SSE-client layer (one place,
        -- not duplicated per listener) avoids per-listener drift. New
        -- event variants added to `SseWireEvent` MUST add a matching
        -- listener registration in the same change; the lack of a
        -- catch-all means a forgotten registration silently degrades
        -- the watchdog rather than producing a compile error.
}

-- REQ-WPV-004: tick check. Fires on a 1-second interval driven by the
-- shared elapsed-counter ticker. Transitions to stale only under the
-- gating conditions; otherwise no-op.
--
-- Note on state names: `live` is the spec-level name in
-- connection_machine.allium (the post-Init healthy state). The UI
-- implementation (`ui/src/hooks/connectionMachine.ts`) calls this state
-- `connected`; `reconnected_display` in the spec maps to `reconnected`
-- in code. Implementers reading these rules should treat
-- `conn/ClientConnection.state = live` as "the connection is healthy
-- enough that absence of events is suspicious" — i.e. `connected` in
-- the UI state machine. `reconnected_display` is excluded by design
-- (the brief grace state after a reconnect; the user is already seeing
-- the "reconnected" badge, additional degraded messaging would be
-- duplicative).
rule WatchdogTick {
    when: ElapsedTickerFired(view)

    requires: HeartbeatWatchdog{view}.freshness = fresh
    requires: conn/ClientConnection{conversation_id: view.conversation_id}.state = live  -- UI code: 'connected'; see ObservedPhase comment above
    requires: ObservedPhase{view}.working = true
    requires: now() - HeartbeatWatchdog{view}.last_event_at
              >= config.heartbeat_watchdog_seconds * 1000

    ensures: HeartbeatWatchdog{view}.freshness = stale
}

-- Disarm when the connection itself reports a problem; the connection
-- chip already conveys the same information and duplicate messaging is
-- worse than one clear signal.
rule WatchdogDisarmsOnConnectionDegrade {
    when: ConnectionStateChanged(view, new_state)

    requires: new_state != live
    requires: HeartbeatWatchdog{view}.freshness = stale

    ensures: HeartbeatWatchdog{view}.freshness = fresh
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Rules — LastKnownActivityCapture
------------------------------------------------------------

-- REQ-WPV-005: on the connected→reconnecting (or →offline) edge, capture
-- the current working activity with its elapsed value frozen.
rule LastKnownActivityCapturedOnDegrade {
    when: ConnectionStateChanged(view, new_state)

    requires: conn/ClientConnection{conversation_id: view.conversation_id}.state = live  -- UI: 'connected', prior state
    requires: new_state in { reconnecting, offline }
    requires: ObservedPhase{view}.working = true
    requires: ObservedPhase{view}.phase != null  -- type-narrowing: implied by working=true, but Allium's optional-typing needs an explicit guard

    -- `current_retry_for(view)` is a helper that returns
    -- `llm_retry/TurnRetryContext{conversation_id:
    -- view.conversation_id}.retry` when that entity exists, or `null`
    -- otherwise. Inlined as a helper (rather than an if-then-else
    -- expression, which the v3 grammar doesn't have) so the snapshot
    -- gets both fields in one value-literal construction.
    let snap = LastKnownActivity{
        phase:                 ObservedPhase{view}.phase,
        base_reason_text:      base_reason_text_for(ObservedPhase{view}),
        elapsed_ms_at_disconnect: now() - ObservedPhase{view}.state_updated_at,
        captured_at:           now(),
        retry:                 current_retry_for(view)
    }

    ensures: LastKnownActivityCapture{view}.captured = snap
}

-- Cleared when a fresh Init replaces ObservedPhase with authoritative
-- current state. Reuses the SseInitReceived trigger; the rule body
-- does not read the payload, only the fact of arrival.
rule LastKnownActivityClearedOnInit {
    when: SseInitReceived(view, raw_state, state_updated_at, pending_truncated)

    ensures: LastKnownActivityCapture{view}.captured = null
}

-- Cleared when the connection enters a "healthy enough" state. The
-- connection_machine transitions reconnecting → reconnected_display
-- (the grace state, where the "Reconnected" badge shows) BEFORE
-- transitioning to live (after RECONNECTED_DISPLAY_DONE fires). Both
-- states represent a successful re-establishment of the SSE stream
-- from the user's POV, so the frozen last-known activity must be
-- cleared on EITHER edge to prevent the "stale captured activity on
-- a healthy connection" failure that LastKnownActivityWellGated forbids.
-- This rule covers the no-Init-yet path: in practice Init always lands
-- on reconnect (LastKnownActivityClearedOnInit handles that), but the
-- reconnect-without-Init defensive clear keeps the invariant tight.
rule LastKnownActivityClearedOnReconnect {
    when: ConnectionStateChanged(view, new_state)

    requires: new_state in { live, reconnected_display }
    requires: LastKnownActivityCapture{view}.captured != null

    ensures: LastKnownActivityCapture{view}.captured = null
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Rules — PendingAssistantBubble
------------------------------------------------------------

-- REQ-WPV-006: enter llm_requesting with no tokens → arm placeholder.
-- The bubble is a reusable singleton, so the precondition admits any
-- non-active state (not_present after the previous turn cleaned up).
-- The placeholder_since stamp is taken from the just-set
-- ObservedPhase.state_updated_at so the inline elapsed counter ticks
-- from phase entry, not from this rule's firing time.
rule PendingBubblePlaceholderCreated {
    when: ObservedPhaseUpdatedToWorking(view, llm_requesting)

    requires: PendingAssistantBubble{view}.state = not_present

    ensures: PendingAssistantBubble{view}.state             = placeholder
    ensures: PendingAssistantBubble{view}.placeholder_since = ObservedPhase{view}.state_updated_at
    ensures: PendingAssistantBubble{view}.first_byte_seq   = null
    -- request_id stays null until LlmFirstByte arrives; the placeholder
    -- bubble doesn't need it for rendering, only the streaming bubble
    -- does (to correlate the persisted Message back to itself).
}

-- REQ-WPV-006 + REQ-WPV-008: a fresh Init that lands while the
-- conversation is in `llm_requesting` and no streaming tokens have
-- arrived yet needs to re-arm the placeholder bubble. The phase-
-- transition trigger `ObservedPhaseUpdatedToWorking` does NOT fire on
-- Init (Init replaces the snapshot wholesale; there is no edge), so
-- without this rule a page reload or reconnect mid-`llm_requesting`
-- would leave the StateBar showing the right phase but the message
-- area missing its in-flight placeholder. The state_updated_at on the
-- Init carrier seeds `placeholder_since` so the elapsed counter
-- continues from the phase entry (not from reload time).
--
-- Gated on `pending_truncated = false`: when the SSE replay ring
-- overflowed, REQ-WPV-008's truncated-branch requires showing a
-- degraded notice in place of inline indicators (the in-flight detail
-- cannot be reliably reconstructed until the next checkpoint).
-- Seeding a fresh-looking placeholder here would conflict with that.
--
-- Event shape: SseInitReceived(view, raw_state, state_updated_at,
-- pending_truncated). `pending_truncated` is the existing
-- `Init.pending_truncated` flag defined in sse_wire.allium.
rule PendingBubbleSeededFromInit {
    when: SseInitReceived(view, raw_state, state_updated_at, pending_truncated)

    requires: is_working_phase(raw_state)
    requires: working_phase_of(raw_state) = llm_requesting
    requires: PendingAssistantBubble{view}.state = not_present
    requires: pending_truncated = false

    ensures: PendingAssistantBubble{view}.state             = placeholder
    ensures: PendingAssistantBubble{view}.placeholder_since = state_updated_at
    ensures: PendingAssistantBubble{view}.first_byte_seq   = null
    ensures: PendingAssistantBubble{view}.request_id        = null
    -- If the server-side turn had already passed first-byte before
    -- reload, the next Token event (replayed from the SSE ring) will
    -- carry the request_id and the regular streaming-transition path
    -- catches up; the bubble is only stuck in `placeholder` for the
    -- pre-first-byte case.
}

-- REQ-WPV-007: LlmFirstByte arrives → transition to streaming. Same DOM
-- node, contents swap from elapsed counter to streamed text. The event
-- carries both `request_id` (correlator the runtime uses internally)
-- and `sequence_id` (the wire-envelope seq, monotonic per stream); we
-- store the seq on the bubble so PendingBubbleCompletedOnMessage can
-- correlate the persisted assistant Message back to this bubble (a
-- Message with role=assistant and seq > first_byte_seq is THIS
-- bubble's completion). request_id alone is unsuitable because
-- SseWireEvent::Message does not carry it.
-- Event shape: SseLlmFirstByteReceived(view, request_id, sequence_id).
rule PendingBubbleTransitionsToStreaming {
    when: SseLlmFirstByteReceived(view, request_id, sequence_id)

    requires: PendingAssistantBubble{view}.state = placeholder

    ensures: PendingAssistantBubble{view}.state           = streaming
    ensures: PendingAssistantBubble{view}.request_id      = request_id
    ensures: PendingAssistantBubble{view}.first_byte_seq = sequence_id
}

-- REQ-WPV-006: phase left llm_requesting without any Token. The bubble
-- returns to `not_present` (NOT a terminal state) so the next
-- llm_requesting entry can re-arm it. Clears the per-bubble fields.
rule PendingBubbleResetOnEmptyPhaseExit {
    when: ObservedPhaseUpdatedFromWorking(view, llm_requesting, new_phase)

    requires: PendingAssistantBubble{view}.state = placeholder

    ensures: PendingAssistantBubble{view}.state             = not_present
    ensures: PendingAssistantBubble{view}.request_id        = null
    ensures: PendingAssistantBubble{view}.placeholder_since = null
    ensures: PendingAssistantBubble{view}.first_byte_seq   = null
}

-- REQ-WPV-006: phase left llm_requesting WHILE the bubble was in
-- `streaming` (some tokens arrived, then the turn errored or was
-- cancelled before the assistant Message was persisted). Without this
-- rule the bubble would stay stuck in `streaming` showing partial
-- text into the error/cancel/retry state, and the next
-- llm_requesting entry would fail the `state = not_present`
-- precondition on PendingBubblePlaceholderCreated.
--
-- The implementation discards the buffered streaming text from the UI
-- on this transition (the partial response is not the canonical
-- output of the turn); a recovery/retry attempt arms a fresh
-- placeholder via the normal phase-transition path.
rule PendingBubbleResetOnStreamingPhaseExit {
    when: ObservedPhaseUpdatedFromWorking(view, llm_requesting, new_phase)

    requires: PendingAssistantBubble{view}.state = streaming

    ensures: PendingAssistantBubble{view}.state             = not_present
    ensures: PendingAssistantBubble{view}.request_id        = null
    ensures: PendingAssistantBubble{view}.placeholder_since = null
    ensures: PendingAssistantBubble{view}.first_byte_seq   = null
}

-- The streaming bubble becomes the canonical persisted message on the
-- next assistant Message event arrival, then returns to `not_present`
-- so the next turn can re-arm. The DOM transition from the live
-- streaming buffer to the canonical persisted message is handled by
-- the implementation; the bubble entity itself just resets.
--
-- Correlation: SseWireEvent::Message payloads do NOT carry request_id
-- (only Token events do). We compare the inbound message's seq to the
-- bubble's stored first_byte_seq (set when the bubble transitioned
-- to streaming). A Message with role=assistant and seq >
-- first_byte_seq is the completion of THIS bubble's request — by
-- SSE sequence_id monotonicity (sse_wire.allium) and the singleton
-- nature of in-flight LLM requests per conversation.
-- Event shape: SseMessageReceived(view, message_role, message_seq).
rule PendingBubbleCompletedOnMessage {
    when: SseMessageReceived(view, message_role, message_seq)

    requires: PendingAssistantBubble{view}.state = streaming
    requires: message_role = assistant
    requires: message_seq > PendingAssistantBubble{view}.first_byte_seq

    ensures: PendingAssistantBubble{view}.state             = not_present
    ensures: PendingAssistantBubble{view}.request_id        = null
    ensures: PendingAssistantBubble{view}.placeholder_since = null
    ensures: PendingAssistantBubble{view}.first_byte_seq   = null
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Rules — InflightToolTimer
------------------------------------------------------------

-- REQ-WPV-002: a per-tool start time appears in a message_updated
-- event. The carrier is the parent assistant message's
-- `display_data.tool_starts` map (HashMap<ToolUseId, unix_ms>): the
-- runtime adds an entry to that map and emits MessageUpdated with the
-- updated display_data when `dispatch_tool_execution` begins. This
-- approach is preferred over amending `ContentBlock::ToolUse` (which is
-- {id, name, input} on disk and crosses all LLM providers); the
-- assistant-message display_data already exists as a structured per-
-- message side-channel for UI metadata (e.g. duration_ms on
-- tool-result messages). See design.md "Per-tool started_at carrier."
-- Event shape: SseToolUseStartedAtUpdated(view, tool_use_id, started_at).
rule InflightToolTimerCreated {
    when: SseToolUseStartedAtUpdated(view, tool_use_id, started_at)

    requires: not exists InflightToolTimer{view: view, tool_use_id: tool_use_id}

    ensures: InflightToolTimer.created(
        view:        view,
        tool_use_id: tool_use_id,
        started_at:  started_at
    )
}

-- Tool result lands → timer removed; the existing duration_ms on the
-- result takes over the display.
-- Event shape: SseToolResultReceived(view, tool_use_id).
rule InflightToolTimerRemovedOnResult {
    when: SseToolResultReceived(view, tool_use_id)

    requires: exists InflightToolTimer{view: view, tool_use_id: tool_use_id}

    ensures: not exists InflightToolTimer{view: view, tool_use_id: tool_use_id}
}

-- Orphan-cleanup paths: an InflightToolTimer is created at dispatch
-- and removed on the matching tool-result event. Several failure
-- modes can leave the timer without a corresponding result event —
-- without explicit cleanup the entity would persist with `started_at`
-- ticking forever in the UI, and a later attempt to recreate it for
-- the same tool_use_id would hit a `not exists` precondition failure
-- on InflightToolTimerCreated. These rules close those holes
-- structurally; the implementation discards the inline DOM timer on
-- the same edges.

-- Conversation reaches a terminal state (Archived, etc.): every
-- in-flight tool timer for the view is removed. The conversation
-- can no longer produce a tool result, so the timer cannot complete
-- via the normal path.
-- Event shape: SseConversationBecameTerminal(view).
rule InflightToolTimerRemovedOnConversationTerminal {
    when: SseConversationBecameTerminal(view)

    ensures: for t in InflightToolTimer{view: view}:
        not exists t
}

-- Phase exited `tool_executing` without the matching tool result —
-- a cancellation that fired before the running tool surfaced its
-- output (cancelling_tool path), or an error that took the conversation
-- out of tool_executing into an error/recovery state. The runtime
-- guarantees no tool result for the cancelled tool, so the timer
-- cannot complete via SseToolResultReceived. Cleared on the phase
-- exit edge.
rule InflightToolTimerRemovedOnToolPhaseExit {
    when: ObservedPhaseUpdatedFromWorking(view, tool_executing, new_phase)

    ensures: for t in InflightToolTimer{view: view}:
        not exists t
}

-- Hard-delete of the conversation removes the per-view state
-- entirely. Mirrors the runtime cascade (REQ-BED-032 in bedrock).
-- Defensive; in practice the ClientView itself is destroyed when the
-- conversation is hard-deleted, so the timers go with it. The rule
-- exists so the invariant holds without depending on actor-destruction
-- ordering.
-- Event shape: SseConversationHardDeleted(view).
rule InflightToolTimerRemovedOnConversationDelete {
    when: SseConversationHardDeleted(view)

    ensures: for t in InflightToolTimer{view: view}:
        not exists t
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Rules — DisplayedActivity derivation
------------------------------------------------------------

-- The StateBar's displayed activity is a pure function of the inputs
-- below. These rules enumerate every case; exactly one fires per
-- evaluation. Evaluated every WATCHDOG_TICK_INTERVAL_MS ms (or on any
-- input change). Per REQ-WPV-003, exactly one live timer in the
-- StateBar at a time — the rules below honor that by construction
-- (no rule produces a text containing more than one elapsed value).

-- The watchdog OVERRIDES other working-state messaging when stale,
-- because the user needs to know the channel is suspect before they
-- trust further detail.
rule DisplayWhenWatchdogStale {
    when: DerivationTriggered(view)

    requires: HeartbeatWatchdog{view}.freshness = stale

    let secs = (now() - HeartbeatWatchdog{view}.last_event_at) / 1000

    ensures: StateBarDisplay{view}.activity = DisplayedActivity{
        text:      "no signal from server for " + str(secs) + "s",
        dot_class: degraded,
        has_timer: true
    }
}

-- REQ-WPV-005: reconnecting with a captured last-known activity.
-- Split into two sibling rules (reconnecting vs offline) because
-- Allium's grammar has no conditional expression — the per-state text
-- and dot_class are baked in per rule.
rule DisplayWhenReconnectingWithCapturedActivity {
    when: DerivationTriggered(view)

    requires: HeartbeatWatchdog{view}.freshness = fresh
    requires: conn/ClientConnection{conversation_id: view.conversation_id}.state = reconnecting
    requires: LastKnownActivityCapture{view}.captured != null

    let snap        = LastKnownActivityCapture{view}.captured
    let elapsed     = snap.elapsed_ms_at_disconnect / 1000
    let attempts    = conn/ClientConnection{conversation_id: view.conversation_id}.attempt
    -- `render_frozen_retry_modifier(snap.retry)` is the helper that
    -- formats the captured llm_retry/RetryContext as " (retry K/N
    -- <reason>)" when snap.retry is non-null, and returns ""
    -- otherwise. Mirrors the live `render_retry_modifier_for(view)`
    -- helper but reads from the frozen snapshot rather than the live
    -- llm_retry/TurnRetryContext, so the "most specific known
    -- activity" survives the disconnect intact (REQ-WPV-003/005).
    let retry_suffix = render_frozen_retry_modifier(snap.retry)

    ensures: StateBarDisplay{view}.activity = DisplayedActivity{
        text:      "reconnecting (" + str(attempts) + ") — last: "
                   + snap.base_reason_text + " " + str(elapsed) + "s"
                   + retry_suffix,
        dot_class: reconnecting,
        has_timer: false
    }
}

rule DisplayWhenOfflineWithCapturedActivity {
    when: DerivationTriggered(view)

    requires: HeartbeatWatchdog{view}.freshness = fresh
    requires: conn/ClientConnection{conversation_id: view.conversation_id}.state = offline
    requires: LastKnownActivityCapture{view}.captured != null

    let snap         = LastKnownActivityCapture{view}.captured
    let elapsed      = snap.elapsed_ms_at_disconnect / 1000
    let retry_suffix = render_frozen_retry_modifier(snap.retry)

    ensures: StateBarDisplay{view}.activity = DisplayedActivity{
        text:      "offline — last: " + snap.base_reason_text
                   + " " + str(elapsed) + "s"
                   + retry_suffix,
        dot_class: offline,
        has_timer: false
    }
}

-- Reconnecting/offline without captured activity (we weren't in a
-- working phase when we lost connection). Defer entirely to the
-- connection-chip messaging; no agent state to surface. `attempt` is
-- the ClientConnection's monotonic counter (see connection_machine
-- ClientConnection.attempt); the `connection_only_display` helper
-- formats this into the connection-chip text the StateBar already
-- renders today.
rule DisplayWhenReconnectingWithoutCapturedActivity {
    when: DerivationTriggered(view)

    requires: HeartbeatWatchdog{view}.freshness = fresh
    requires: conn/ClientConnection{conversation_id: view.conversation_id}.state in { reconnecting, offline }
    requires: LastKnownActivityCapture{view}.captured = null

    let conn_state = conn/ClientConnection{conversation_id: view.conversation_id}.state
    let attempts   = conn/ClientConnection{conversation_id: view.conversation_id}.attempt

    ensures: StateBarDisplay{view}.activity = connection_only_display(conn_state, attempts)
}

-- Transient connection states: `connecting` (first SSE open),
-- `reconnected_display` (the brief grace state right after a successful
-- reconnect — the user is seeing the "Reconnected" badge), and
-- `disconnected` (between unmount and the next mount). These are
-- excluded from `state = live` and so would otherwise fall through
-- every DisplayWhen* branch, leaving StateBarDisplay stale or
-- undefined. Defer to `connection_only_display(state, attempts)` for
-- the StateBar text — the connection chip already conveys the state
-- itself and the rule below ensures every connection-state value has
-- exactly one matching DisplayWhen* branch by construction.
rule DisplayWhenConnectionTransient {
    when: DerivationTriggered(view)

    requires: HeartbeatWatchdog{view}.freshness = fresh
    requires: conn/ClientConnection{conversation_id: view.conversation_id}.state
              in { connecting, reconnected_display, disconnected }

    let conn_state = conn/ClientConnection{conversation_id: view.conversation_id}.state
    let attempts   = conn/ClientConnection{conversation_id: view.conversation_id}.attempt

    ensures: StateBarDisplay{view}.activity = connection_only_display(conn_state, attempts)
}

-- REQ-WPV-007: streaming sub-phase — no elapsed counter.
rule DisplayWhenStreaming {
    when: DerivationTriggered(view)

    requires: HeartbeatWatchdog{view}.freshness = fresh
    requires: conn/ClientConnection{conversation_id: view.conversation_id}.state = live  -- UI code: 'connected'; see ObservedPhase comment above
    requires: ObservedPhase{view}.working = true
    requires: ObservedPhase{view}.phase = llm_requesting
    requires: PendingAssistantBubble{view}.state = streaming

    let retry_suffix = render_retry_modifier_for(view)

    ensures: StateBarDisplay{view}.activity = DisplayedActivity{
        text:      "streaming" + retry_suffix,
        dot_class: working,
        has_timer: false
    }
}

-- REQ-WPV-003 / REQ-WPV-007: pre-first-byte llm_requesting → "thinking Ns".
rule DisplayWhenThinking {
    when: DerivationTriggered(view)

    requires: HeartbeatWatchdog{view}.freshness = fresh
    requires: conn/ClientConnection{conversation_id: view.conversation_id}.state = live  -- UI code: 'connected'; see ObservedPhase comment above
    requires: ObservedPhase{view}.working = true
    requires: ObservedPhase{view}.phase = llm_requesting
    requires: PendingAssistantBubble{view}.state in { not_present, placeholder }

    let secs         = (now() - ObservedPhase{view}.state_updated_at) / 1000
    let retry_suffix = render_retry_modifier_for(view)

    ensures: StateBarDisplay{view}.activity = DisplayedActivity{
        text:      "thinking " + str(secs) + "s" + retry_suffix,
        dot_class: working,
        has_timer: true
    }
}

-- REQ-WPV-003: tool_executing → "executing <tool_name> Ns" when an
-- InflightToolTimer exists for the view (the timer's tool_use_id
-- identifies the active tool). If multiple timers exist (parallel
-- dispatch — currently not supported), the most recently started one
-- wins per current_tool_name's docs.
rule DisplayWhenToolExecutingWithTimer {
    when: DerivationTriggered(view)

    requires: HeartbeatWatchdog{view}.freshness = fresh
    requires: conn/ClientConnection{conversation_id: view.conversation_id}.state = live  -- UI code: 'connected'; see ObservedPhase comment above
    requires: ObservedPhase{view}.working = true
    requires: ObservedPhase{view}.phase = tool_executing
    requires: exists InflightToolTimer{view: view}

    let secs         = (now() - ObservedPhase{view}.state_updated_at) / 1000
    let tool_name    = current_tool_name(view)
    let retry_suffix = render_retry_modifier_for(view)

    ensures: StateBarDisplay{view}.activity = DisplayedActivity{
        text:      "executing " + tool_name + " " + str(secs) + "s" + retry_suffix,
        dot_class: working,
        has_timer: true
    }
}

-- Brief no-timer window inside tool_executing. The runtime's transition
-- order is `Effect::NotifyStateChange` (sets phase=tool_executing on
-- the wire) then `Effect::ExecuteTool` (which emits the MessageUpdated
-- that creates the InflightToolTimer). In between, the rule above is
-- inapplicable (`exists InflightToolTimer` fails); this rule covers
-- the gap with a tool-name-less display so the StateBar remains
-- defined. Elapsed time is still server-authoritative
-- (state_updated_at). The window closes within one frame in practice
-- (both effects fire from the same `apply_transition_result`
-- invocation), so the user typically sees "executing <name> Ns"
-- without ever observing the fallback; the rule exists for
-- correctness, not UX.
rule DisplayWhenToolExecutingNoTimerYet {
    when: DerivationTriggered(view)

    requires: HeartbeatWatchdog{view}.freshness = fresh
    requires: conn/ClientConnection{conversation_id: view.conversation_id}.state = live
    requires: ObservedPhase{view}.working = true
    requires: ObservedPhase{view}.phase = tool_executing
    requires: not exists InflightToolTimer{view: view}

    let secs         = (now() - ObservedPhase{view}.state_updated_at) / 1000
    let retry_suffix = render_retry_modifier_for(view)

    ensures: StateBarDisplay{view}.activity = DisplayedActivity{
        text:      "executing " + str(secs) + "s" + retry_suffix,
        dot_class: working,
        has_timer: true
    }
}

-- Fallback for the other working phases (awaiting_sub_agents,
-- awaiting_continuation, cancelling, awaiting_recovery). One rule
-- generates the text via a phase-to-prose helper; the timer behavior
-- is uniform.
rule DisplayWhenOtherWorking {
    when: DerivationTriggered(view)

    requires: HeartbeatWatchdog{view}.freshness = fresh
    requires: conn/ClientConnection{conversation_id: view.conversation_id}.state = live  -- UI code: 'connected'; see ObservedPhase comment above
    requires: ObservedPhase{view}.working = true
    requires: ObservedPhase{view}.phase not in { llm_requesting, tool_executing }

    let secs         = (now() - ObservedPhase{view}.state_updated_at) / 1000
    let prose        = phase_prose(ObservedPhase{view}.phase)
    let retry_suffix = render_retry_modifier_for(view)

    ensures: StateBarDisplay{view}.activity = DisplayedActivity{
        text:      prose + " " + str(secs) + "s" + retry_suffix,
        dot_class: working,
        has_timer: true
    }
}

-- Idle / terminal / approval / error: defer to the existing phase
-- text. No live timer.
rule DisplayWhenNotWorking {
    when: DerivationTriggered(view)

    requires: HeartbeatWatchdog{view}.freshness = fresh
    requires: conn/ClientConnection{conversation_id: view.conversation_id}.state = live  -- UI code: 'connected'; see ObservedPhase comment above
    requires: ObservedPhase{view}.working = false

    ensures: StateBarDisplay{view}.activity = non_working_display(ObservedPhase{view})
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Invariants
------------------------------------------------------------

-- REQ-WPV-003: exactly one live elapsed counter in the StateBar.
invariant SingleLiveTimerInStateBar {
    for v in ClientView:
        live_timer_count_in(StateBarDisplay{view: v}.activity.text) <= 1
}

-- REQ-WPV-001: elapsed time is ALWAYS derived from a server-authoritative
-- timestamp. If a UI elapsed value exists, it must trace to either
-- ObservedPhase.state_updated_at, InflightToolTimer.started_at, or
-- HeartbeatWatchdog.last_event_at (the watchdog is client-side by
-- construction — it measures local silence).
invariant ElapsedTracesToServerTimestamp {
    for v in ClientView:
        for elapsed in elapsed_values_in(StateBarDisplay{view: v}):
            elapsed.source in {
                ObservedPhase{view: v}.state_updated_at,
                any InflightToolTimer{view: v}.started_at,
                HeartbeatWatchdog{view: v}.last_event_at
            }
}

-- REQ-WPV-005: LastKnownActivity is present iff we are in a degraded
-- connection state AND were working when we degraded.
invariant LastKnownActivityWellGated {
    for v in ClientView:
        LastKnownActivityCapture{view: v}.captured != null
        implies conn/ClientConnection{conversation_id: v.conversation_id}.state in { reconnecting, offline }
}

-- REQ-WPV-005: a fresh Init wipes any stale frozen activity (the
-- captured last-known activity is for display-during-disconnect; when
-- the next Init lands, the live phase is authoritative again).
invariant InitClearsCapturedActivity {
    for v in ClientView:
        most_recent_event_was_init(v)
        implies LastKnownActivityCapture{view: v}.captured = null
}

-- REQ-WPV-006: the placeholder bubble is bound to a llm_requesting phase.
invariant PlaceholderBubbleImpliesLlmRequesting {
    for v in ClientView:
        PendingAssistantBubble{view: v}.state = placeholder
        implies (ObservedPhase{view: v}.working = true
                 and ObservedPhase{view: v}.phase = llm_requesting)
}

-- REQ-WPV-004: the watchdog can be stale only while the connection is
-- live and the phase is working. The disarm-on-degrade rule enforces
-- this; the invariant makes it structural.
invariant WatchdogStaleOnlyWhenWorkingAndLive {
    for v in ClientView where HeartbeatWatchdog{view: v}.freshness = stale:
        conn/ClientConnection{conversation_id: v.conversation_id}.state = live
        and ObservedPhase{view: v}.working = true
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Surfaces
------------------------------------------------------------

-- The single surface this spec exposes to the rendering layer. The
-- StateBar component reads StateBarDisplay; the MessageList reads
-- PendingAssistantBubble and InflightToolTimer to render the inline
-- indicators. The composition machinery (rules above) is encapsulated
-- — consumers do not access ObservedPhase, HeartbeatWatchdog, or
-- LastKnownActivityCapture directly.
surface ConversationActivityFeed {
    facing user_view: ClientView

    exposes:
        StateBarDisplay{view: user_view}
        PendingAssistantBubble{view: user_view}.state
        PendingAssistantBubble{view: user_view}.placeholder_since
        PendingAssistantBubble{view: user_view}.request_id
        InflightToolTimer{view: user_view}.started_at  -- one per tool_use_id

    @guarantee SingleSourceOfElapsedTime
        -- Every elapsed value visible to the user traces back to a
        -- server-authoritative timestamp (state_updated_at, started_at) OR to
        -- the watchdog's local silence measurement. No elapsed value is
        -- computed from event-arrival time.

    @guarantee NoMaskedActivity
        -- During any connection-degraded state, if the agent was in a
        -- working phase at the moment of degrade, the user sees BOTH
        -- the connection state AND the captured last-known activity.

    @guarantee SingleStateBarTimer
        -- The StateBar contains at most one live elapsed counter. Inline
        -- per-artifact timers (tool widget, pending bubble) are
        -- structurally separate and do not count against this guarantee.

    @guarantee NoSilentLongWait
        -- During any working phase with a healthy SSE connection, if no
        -- SSE event of any kind arrives for HEARTBEAT_WATCHDOG_SECONDS,
        -- the user sees a degraded-signal indicator. The "no event"
        -- check includes server-typed `ping` keep-alives, so a healthy
        -- but slow LLM stream does not trigger a false positive.
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Deferred
------------------------------------------------------------

deferred MultipleParallelToolsInOneAssistantMessage
    -- The runtime currently dispatches tool calls sequentially within a
    -- turn. If parallel dispatch arrives, the per-tool InflightToolTimer
    -- entity already supports it (each tool has its own started_at);
    -- only the DisplayWhenToolExecuting rule's `current_tool_name(view)`
    -- helper needs revisiting (most-recently-started vs longest-running
    -- vs all-aggregated). Defer the policy choice until the use case
    -- materialises.
    -- Location: ui/src/components/StateBar.tsx

deferred AggregateActivityDashboard
    -- A cross-conversation view ("which conversations have stuck agents,
    -- by reason") is potentially useful for operators but out of scope
    -- for v1. The per-conversation indicators in this spec are the
    -- precondition for any such aggregate view.
    -- Location: would live in ui/src/pages/

deferred PerArtifactRetryBadge
    -- Per REQ-LRV-007 the retry badge lives on the assistant message
    -- bubble. Equivalent inline badges on tool widgets ("this tool
    -- call's underlying LLM turn retried 2x") would require correlating
    -- retry events to specific tool blocks; defer.
    -- Location: ui/src/components/MessageComponents.tsx

deferred Req008ReloadContinuity
    -- REQ-WPV-008 ("display continuity across reload, within 1s of
    -- continuous-connect") is an emergent property of:
    --   (a) REQ-WPV-001's server-authoritative state_updated_at being
    --       carried on Init and StateChange (ObservedPhaseSeededFromInit
    --       + ObservedPhaseUpdatedByStateChange rules above), and
    --   (b) the pending_truncated=true degraded-display branch
    --       documented in requirements.md, which reads from sse_wire's
    --       InitSnapshot.pending_truncated flag.
    -- The acceptance-criterion expression of REQ-WPV-008 lives in
    -- requirements.md (the WHEN/THEN pair with the pending_truncated
    -- branch); modelling it as an Allium rule here would duplicate
    -- existing entity assignments without adding new behavioural
    -- structure. The integration test that proves REQ-WPV-008 will
    -- exercise the entity-assignment rules above plus the
    -- ConversationActivityFeed surface guarantees.
    -- Location: ui/src/conversation/atom.ts (Init reducer path),
    -- and sse_wire.allium's InitSnapshot.pending_truncated.

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Open questions
------------------------------------------------------------

-- No open questions remain. Decisions resolved during elicitation
-- session dated 2026-05-25:
--
--   - state_updated_at: server-authoritative on both StateChange and Init's
--     phase. Client-side timestamps explicitly rejected because they
--     reset on reconnect/reload and diverge across tabs.
--
--   - StateBar composition: base reason + optional retry-modifier;
--     exactly one live timer at a time; retry is a modifier (not a
--     replacement) of the base reason. Multiple parallel timers
--     explicitly rejected as visual noise.
--
--   - Heartbeat watchdog threshold: 35s (2.3x the 15s server keep-alive
--     interval). Triggers only when conn.state = live AND phase is
--     working AND no SSE event of any kind has arrived. The "any kind"
--     scope requires switching the server keep-alive from an SSE
--     comment to a typed `event: ping` so the client EventSource
--     observes it. Documented in design.md.
--
--   - Reconnect display: BOTH connection chip AND last-known activity,
--     with elapsed FROZEN at disconnect (not advancing through the
--     reconnect — honest about what we don't know). Tooltip-only
--     surfacing of last-known activity explicitly rejected as
--     against the project's information-density principle.
--
--   - First-byte split: `streaming` displays without elapsed counter;
--     the stream itself is the progress signal and an additional
--     counter is redundant.
--
--   - Pending assistant bubble: placeholder bubble appears at the
--     bottom of the conversation during llm_requesting with no tokens;
--     contents swap from elapsed counter to streamed text on first
--     token without DOM remount. Implemented as a synthetic
--     `pending_agent` tail unit in `ui/src/conversation/renderUnits.ts`
--     (parallel to the existing `streaming_agent` unit), NOT by
--     amending the empty-message filter at MessageComponents.tsx —
--     no assistant message row exists in the messages table during
--     pre-first-byte llm_requesting (responses are persisted only
--     after LlmResponse), so there is nothing to retain via filter
--     amendment. The empty-message filter is left unchanged. See
--     design.md "Pending assistant bubble" for the reasoning.
--
--   - Per-tool started_at carrier: a typed `tool_starts: BTreeMap<
--     String, i64>` field on the assistant message's display_data,
--     populated by the runtime when `dispatch_tool_execution` begins
--     and propagated via `MessageUpdated`. Mirrors the duration_ms
--     convention (typed metadata on message display_data). A new field
--     on `ContentBlock::ToolUse` was rejected because that struct is
--     persisted/cross-provider and adding a UI-side field there
--     requires a migration. A new ToolExecutionStarted SSE variant was
--     rejected as a parallel representation of the same value.
--
--   - State-entry timestamp: reuse the existing
--     `Conversation.state_updated_at: DateTime<Utc>` (already bumped on
--     every state transition via db.rs:676) rather than introducing a
--     parallel `entered_at` field. On Init the value is already at the
--     top of `init.conversation` via the `#[serde(flatten)]` on
--     `EnrichedConversation`; on StateChange we add a typed
--     `state_updated_at: DateTime<Utc>` field carrying the same value
--     (RFC3339 on the wire to match the Init flatten; client converts
--     to ms once at the SSE-handler boundary).
